,{
"ClauseCode":"1017807"
,"ClauseContent":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:9px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\">Each item insured under this memorandum is declared to be separately subject to the following&nbsp;<br />\ncondition of average namely :&nbsp;<br />\nIf at the time of reinstatement the sum representing less that eighty (80%) percent of the cost which would have been incurred in reinstatement if the whole of the property covered by such item had been destroyed exceeds the sum insured herein at the breaking out of any fire or at the commencement of any destruction of or damage to such property by any other peril hereby incurred against, then the insured shall be considered as being his own insurer for the difference between the sum insured and the sum representing the cost of reinstatement of the whole of the property and shall bear a rateable proportion of the loss accordingly.</span></span></p>"
,"ClauseDescription":"Average Relief Clause (80%)"
,"ClauseTitle":"Average Relief Clause (80%)"
